# Unit11
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit11核心词汇

method/ˈmeθəd/方法/This is an effective method of learning.
migrate/maɪˈɡreɪt/迁移/Many birds migrate south in winter.
military/ˈmɪlɪteri/军事的/He served in the military for ten years.
minister/ˈmɪnɪstər/部长/The prime minister gave a speech.
minor/ˈmaɪnər/较小的/This is a minor problem; don't worry.
minority/maɪˈnɔːrəti/少数/Only a minority of people opposed the plan.
miracle/ˈmɪrəkl/奇迹/It was a miracle that no one was hurt.
mission/ˈmɪʃn/任务/They completed the mission successfully.
moderate/ˈmɑːdərət/适度的/Do moderate exercise every day.
modify/ˈmɑːdɪfaɪ/修改/We need to modify the plan slightly.
monitor/ˈmɑːnɪtər/监控/The nurse monitored the patient's condition.
moral/ˈmɔːrəl/道德的/He is a man of high moral standards.
moreover/mɔːrˈoʊvər/此外/The plan is too expensive; moreover, it is impractical.
motive/ˈmoʊtɪv/动机/What was his motive for committing the crime?
multiple/ˈmʌltɪpl/多个的/He has multiple talents.
mutual/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/相互的/They have mutual respect for each other.
narrative/ˈnærətɪv/叙述/The narrative of the novel is very engaging.
neglect/nɪˈɡlekt/忽视/Don't neglect your health.
negotiate/nɪˈɡoʊʃieɪt/谈判/The two sides are negotiating a peace deal.
neutral/ˈnjuːtrəl/中立的/Switzerland remained neutral during the war.
nevertheless/ˌnevərðəˈles/然而/The task was difficult; nevertheless, we completed it.
noble/ˈnoʊbl/高尚的/He is a man of noble character.
norm/nɔːrm/规范/Social norms vary from culture to culture.
notable/ˈnoʊtəbl/值得注意的/There has been a notable improvement in her work.
notion/ˈnoʊʃn/概念/The notion of equality is fundamental to democracy.
notorious/noʊˈtɔːriəs/臭名昭著的/The area is notorious for its high crime rate.
nuclear/ˈnjuːkliər/核的/Nuclear energy is a controversial topic.
numerous/ˈnuːmərəs/众多的/Numerous studies support this theory.
nutrition/njuˈtrɪʃn/营养/Good nutrition is essential for health.
obey/oˈbeɪ/服从/You must obey the rules.
objective/əbˈdʒektɪv/目标/Our main objective is to improve quality.
obligation/ˌɑːblɪˈɡeɪʃn/义务/It is our obligation to protect the environment.
oblige/əˈblaɪdʒ/迫使/The law obliges companies to pay taxes.
observe/əbˈzɜːrv/观察/Scientists observe the stars through telescopes.
obstacle/ˈɑːbstəkl/障碍/Lack of funding is a major obstacle.
obtain/əbˈteɪn/获得/She obtained a degree in engineering.
obvious/ˈɑːbviəs/明显的/It was obvious that he was lying.
occupation/ˌɑːkjuˈpeɪʃn/职业/What is your occupation?
occupy/ˈɑːkjupaɪ/占据/The meeting occupied the whole morning.
occur/əˈkɜːr/发生/The accident occurred at midnight.
offend/əˈfend/冒犯/I'm sorry if I offended you.
offense/əˈfens/冒犯；犯罪/He was charged with a serious offense.
operate/ˈɑːpəreɪt/操作/Do you know how to operate this machine?
opponent/əˈpoʊnənt/对手/He defeated his opponent in the match.
opportunity/ˌɑːpərˈtuːnəti/机会/This is a great opportunity for you.
oppose/əˈpoʊz/反对/Many people opposed the new policy.
optimistic/ˌɑːptɪˈmɪstɪk/乐观的/She is optimistic about the future.
option/ˈɑːpʃn/选择/You have several options to choose from.
orient/ˈɔːrient/使适应/She oriented herself to the new environment.
origin/ˈɔːrɪdʒɪn/起源/The origin of this tradition dates back centuries.
